# 32. Construct Binary Tree from Postorder and Inorder

**a2z-330**

Postorder:

```text
left → right → root
```

So process postorder **from right to left**.

## Java

```java
public static TreeNode buildTree(
        int[] inorder,
        int[] postorder) {

    Map<Integer, Integer> index = new HashMap<>();

    for (int i = 0; i < inorder.length; i++)
        index.put(inorder[i], i);

    int[] postIndex = {postorder.length - 1};

    return build(
        inorder,
        postorder,
        0,
        inorder.length - 1,
        postIndex,
        index
    );
}

private static TreeNode build(
        int[] inorder,
        int[] postorder,
        int left,
        int right,
        int[] postIndex,
        Map<Integer, Integer> index) {

    if (left > right)
        return null;

    int value = postorder[postIndex[0]--];

    TreeNode root = new TreeNode(value);

    int mid = index.get(value);

    // Because postorder is processed backwards:
    // build right subtree before left subtree.
    root.right = build(
        inorder, postorder,
        mid + 1, right,
        postIndex, index
    );

    root.left = build(
        inorder, postorder,
        left, mid - 1,
        postIndex, index
    );

    return root;
}
```

## C#

