# 10. Preorder + Inorder + Postorder in One Traversal

**a2z-308**

Use a stack containing:

```text
(node, state)
```

State:

```text
1 → preorder
2 → inorder
3 → postorder
```

## Java

```java
static class Pair {
    TreeNode node;
    int state;

    Pair(TreeNode node, int state) {
        this.node = node;
        this.state = state;
    }
}

public static void allTraversals(
        TreeNode root,
        List<Integer> pre,
        List<Integer> in,
        List<Integer> post) {

    if (root == null)
        return;

    Stack<Pair> stack = new Stack<>();
    stack.push(new Pair(root, 1));

    while (!stack.isEmpty()) {

        Pair current = stack.peek();

        if (current.state == 1) {

            // First time -> preorder.
            pre.add(current.node.val);

            current.state++;

            if (current.node.left != null)
                stack.push(
                    new Pair(current.node.left, 1)
                );

        }
        else if (current.state == 2) {

            // Returning from left -> inorder.
            in.add(current.node.val);

            current.state++;

            if (current.node.right != null)
                stack.push(
                    new Pair(current.node.right, 1)
                );

        }
        else {

            // Returning from both subtrees -> postorder.
            post.add(current.node.val);

            stack.pop();
        }
    }
}
```

