# 9. Postorder Traversal Using 1 Stack

**a2z-307**

## Java

```java
public static List<Integer> postorderOneStack(
        TreeNode root) {

    List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();

    Stack<TreeNode> stack = new Stack<>();
    TreeNode current = root;
    TreeNode lastVisited = null;

    while (current != null || !stack.isEmpty()) {

        if (current != null) {
            // Go as far left as possible.
            stack.push(current);
            current = current.left;
        }
        else {
            TreeNode peek = stack.peek();

            // Right subtree still needs processing.
            if (peek.right != null &&
                lastVisited != peek.right) {

                current = peek.right;
            }
            else {
                // Both children processed.
                result.add(peek.val);
                lastVisited = stack.pop();
            }
        }
    }

    return result;
}
```

