# 1. Pre, Inorder and Postorder in One Traversal

**a2z-299**

This is essentially the recursive version of the state-machine problem.

## Java

```java
static class Traversals {
    List<Integer> preorder = new ArrayList<>();
    List<Integer> inorder = new ArrayList<>();
    List<Integer> postorder = new ArrayList<>();
}

public static Traversals allTraversals(
        TreeNode root) {

    Traversals result = new Traversals();

    dfs(root, result);

    return result;
}

private static void dfs(
        TreeNode root,
        Traversals result) {

    if (root == null)
        return;

    // First position -> preorder.
    result.preorder.add(root.val);

    dfs(root.left, result);

    // After left subtree -> inorder.
    result.inorder.add(root.val);

    dfs(root.right, result);

    // After both subtrees -> postorder.
    result.postorder.add(root.val);
}
```

